From: Elian Doran <doran.adoris.elian@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: axp20x_battery: PinePhone: input current limit 3 A

The AXP803 keeps its input current limit across reboots, and nothing in
this firmware sets it: whatever ran before decides. After BC1.2 detection
ran once (axp20x_usb_power enables it), the limit stayed at 500 mA for a
PC's port, less than the phone draws with the screen on, so the battery
barely charged or slowly discharged while plugged in.
Set 3 A at boot, as the PMIC held before; once a cable is connected the
ANX7688 driver sets what the port advertises.
previous patch keeps a weak port from being overloaded.

---
--- a/drivers/power/supply/axp20x_battery.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/axp20x_battery.c
@@ -1213,6 +1213,17 @@
 		ret = regmap_update_bits(axp20x_batt->regmap, 0x30, 0x7 << 3, 0x3 << 3);
 		if (ret)
 			goto warn_bat;
+
+		/*
+		 * Input current limit 3 A (0x35 bits 7:4 = 6, as axp20x_usb_power's
+		 * table). The PMIC keeps it across reboots: BC1.2 detection, which
+		 * axp20x_usb_power enables, set 500 mA on a PC's port and charging
+		 * stayed starved after it. The ANX7688 driver then sets what the port
+		 * advertises.
+		 */
+		ret = regmap_update_bits(axp20x_batt->regmap, 0x35, 0xf << 4, 0x6 << 4);
+		if (ret)
+			goto warn_bat;
 	}
 
 	return 0;
